; Next decimal digit by repeated subtraction
;
; Divides HL by DE with a loop of subtractions and returns the quotient as an
; ASCII digit (the quotient must be below 10). The caller prints the digit
; with #R$858B, skipping it when it is "0" for the leading hundreds place of
; the score.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; HL Number
; DE Divisor (100, then 10)
; O:A ASCII digit "0"-"9"
; O:HL Remainder
; O:F Z set when the digit is "0"
@label=DecimalDigit
@isub=LD A,'0'-1
c$842E LD A,$2F
*$8430 INC A
 $8431 AND A
 $8432 SBC HL,DE
 $8434 JR NC,$8430
 $8436 ADD HL,DE
@isub=CP '0'
 $8437 CP $30
 $8439 RET
